{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q1321290","formula":"C₄H₅N","hill":"C4H5N","elements":["H","C","N"],"composition":{"C":4.0,"H":5.0,"N":1.0},"names":{"en":"Allyl cyanide","ru":"Аллилцианид"},"descriptions":{"en":"Allyl cyanide is an organic compound with the formula CH2CHCH2CN. Like other small alkyl nitriles, allyl cyanide is colorless and soluble in organic solvents. Allyl cyanide occurs naturally as an antifeedant and is used as a cross-linking agent in some polymers.","ru":"Аллилцианид (3-бутеннитрил) — органическое соединение с химической формулой CH2=CHCH2CN. Представляет собой бесцветную жидкость, которая легко растворяется в органических растворителях. Образует азеотропные смеси с водой, а также с водой и аллиловым спиртом."},"fame":14,"pubchemCid":8009,"mass":67.09,"charge":0,"smiles":"C=CCC#N","inchikey":"SJNALLRHIVGIBI-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"but-3-enenitrile","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"8009","atoms":10,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":-2.229,"y":0.468,"z":-0.007,"el":"N"},{"x":0.059,"y":-0.821,"z":-0.116,"el":"C"},{"x":1.158,"y":0.03,"z":0.439,"el":"C"},{"x":2.229,"y":0.42,"z":-0.262,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.217,"y":-0.098,"z":-0.054,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.007,"y":-1.743,"z":0.472,"el":"H"},{"x":0.268,"y":-1.115,"z":-1.151,"el":"H"},{"x":1.087,"y":0.331,"z":1.482,"el":"H"},{"x":2.997,"y":1.03,"z":0.201,"el":"H"},{"x":2.358,"y":0.142,"z":-1.302,"el":"H"}],"bonds":[[0,4,3],[1,2,1],[1,4,1],[1,5,1],[1,6,1],[2,3,2],[2,7,1],[3,8,1],[3,9,1]]},"sources":[{"role":"identity","name":"Wikidata","url":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q1321290","license":"CC0 1.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (en)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Allyl_cyanide","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (ru)","url":"https://ru.wikipedia.org/wi